1
00:02:39,440 --> 00:02:42,160
Father! Da's been shot.

2
00:02:42,240 --> 00:02:45,640
She's lost a lot of blood.
Does anyone share Ms. Nada's blood type?

3
00:02:45,720 --> 00:02:46,520
Rawee does.

4
00:02:47,160 --> 00:02:48,520
<i>Uncle, how did you know</i>

5
00:02:48,600 --> 00:02:50,720
Mr. Rawee's blood type matches Aunt Da's?

6
00:02:50,800 --> 00:02:52,040
Well…

7
00:02:52,880 --> 00:02:54,560
I've known this family for a long time.

8
00:02:54,640 --> 00:02:56,920
You hired someone to shoot her,
didn't you?

9
00:02:57,000 --> 00:03:00,000
Why would I do that?
More likely, it was you.

10
00:03:00,080 --> 00:03:01,160
Why would I?

11
00:03:01,240 --> 00:03:02,680
That news about the fortune teller,

12
00:03:02,760 --> 00:03:04,680
didn't Da leak it

13
00:03:04,760 --> 00:03:05,840
to get back at you?

14
00:03:07,120 --> 00:03:08,280
That bitch, Nada.

15
00:03:08,360 --> 00:03:09,800
"THE HEART OF SUCCESS IS HAPPINESS"
NADA TAYAWAT

16
00:03:09,880 --> 00:03:11,440
MAY 12 - DEAR DIARY,
TODAY I ALMOST CRIED IN FRONT OF FATHER

17
00:03:11,520 --> 00:03:12,440
"Times change."

18
00:03:13,120 --> 00:03:14,520
"People change."

19
00:03:14,600 --> 00:03:16,160
Are those documents for Aunt Pim?

20
00:03:16,240 --> 00:03:17,480
Well…

21
00:03:17,560 --> 00:03:21,360
I know they're very important.

22
00:03:21,920 --> 00:03:24,040
I'll hand them to her myself.

23
00:03:24,680 --> 00:03:26,840
Please make sure she gets them.

24
00:03:28,120 --> 00:03:29,360
Of course.

25
00:03:36,920 --> 00:03:39,760
-Hello?
-Where's Taddao?

26
00:03:40,520 --> 00:03:42,200
She's on her lunch break.

27
00:03:42,920 --> 00:03:44,920
If you need anything,
I'd be happy to help.

28
00:03:48,400 --> 00:03:49,240
Yes, Sir.

29
00:03:59,040 --> 00:03:59,920
Come in.

30
00:04:20,079 --> 00:04:21,360
Your coffee, Sir.

31
00:04:23,000 --> 00:04:26,160
How did you know
I take black coffee with dark chocolate?

32
00:04:28,360 --> 00:04:30,240
I called Taddao to ask.

33
00:04:35,200 --> 00:04:36,960
You know how to get on my good side.

34
00:04:44,840 --> 00:04:46,480
You really do look like Rawich.

35
00:04:49,640 --> 00:04:53,000
Who's Rawich?

36
00:04:56,360 --> 00:04:57,840
My former secretary.

37
00:04:59,120 --> 00:05:02,120
Nada's husband. He died a long time ago.

38
00:05:08,200 --> 00:05:10,640
You're very close to Phakorn, aren't you?

39
00:05:12,520 --> 00:05:15,400
Yes. We grew up together.

40
00:05:18,520 --> 00:05:20,320
Nada asked you to work here, didn't she?

41
00:05:22,320 --> 00:05:23,280
Yes, Sir.

42
00:05:27,080 --> 00:05:28,320
Maybe

43
00:05:29,240 --> 00:05:31,640
you remind her of her late husband.

44
00:05:34,000 --> 00:05:35,920
That could be why she's so fond of you.

45
00:05:44,840 --> 00:05:46,080
Who named you?

46
00:05:48,600 --> 00:05:49,680
My mother.

47
00:05:58,000 --> 00:06:00,160
Your names are so similar.

48
00:06:03,760 --> 00:06:04,960
Quite a coincidence.

49
00:06:10,280 --> 00:06:12,200
You can get back to work now.

50
00:06:15,360 --> 00:06:16,440
Yes, Sir.

51
00:06:53,240 --> 00:06:54,800
Look at you.

52
00:07:07,000 --> 00:07:10,400
Hello? The DNA results are in?

53
00:07:11,360 --> 00:07:13,360
Is Phakorn Nada's son?

54
00:07:15,920 --> 00:07:17,200
He isn't?

55
00:07:17,840 --> 00:07:19,240
No match at all?

56
00:07:20,880 --> 00:07:21,960
Are you sure?

57
00:07:22,560 --> 00:07:24,640
What about Rawee?

58
00:07:25,240 --> 00:07:27,120
Does his DNA match Nada's?

59
00:07:29,400 --> 00:07:30,680
No?

60
00:07:32,080 --> 00:07:33,040
Well…

61
00:07:33,680 --> 00:07:34,920
I see.

62
00:07:36,760 --> 00:07:38,520
Where are the results now?

63
00:07:42,000 --> 00:07:45,320
You left them with…? Oh, okay.

64
00:07:45,400 --> 00:07:48,840
I'll come get them right away. Bye.

65
00:08:00,120 --> 00:08:02,160
Mother and son both put on quite an act.

66
00:08:03,440 --> 00:08:06,200
Just you wait. This time,

67
00:08:06,280 --> 00:08:09,000
I'll bring you down, Nada.

68
00:08:25,800 --> 00:08:26,760
DR. THONGPHUM KHUMDEE

69
00:08:30,560 --> 00:08:31,720
A nurse asked me to give you this.

70
00:08:35,760 --> 00:08:37,840
I'll head home, then.

71
00:08:37,919 --> 00:08:41,240
Nada's asleep.
I wouldn't get to talk to her anyway.

72
00:08:42,640 --> 00:08:43,600
Alright.

73
00:10:25,680 --> 00:10:27,680
Hello, Alyssa.

74
00:10:28,440 --> 00:10:30,080
Hello, Auntie.

75
00:10:31,080 --> 00:10:33,000
Are you here to visit Mr. Rawee?

76
00:10:33,880 --> 00:10:36,320
Yes. Would you like to come in for a chat?

77
00:10:36,400 --> 00:10:38,640
Wee's at work. He's not back yet.

78
00:10:40,920 --> 00:10:41,880
I'd love to.

79
00:11:09,120 --> 00:11:13,000
I actually came to visit Ms. Nada.
I'm heading back this evening.

80
00:11:15,120 --> 00:11:18,160
Is that a photo of Mr. Rawee and Phakorn
when they were little?

81
00:11:20,080 --> 00:11:22,480
Yes. Oh.

82
00:11:23,080 --> 00:11:25,840
Why don't you call him Wee?
Just call him Wee.

83
00:11:25,920 --> 00:11:27,800
You don't have to be so formal.

84
00:11:29,560 --> 00:11:30,920
I'm used to it.

85
00:11:36,720 --> 00:11:38,160
That hat…

86
00:11:42,560 --> 00:11:45,280
My mom says you'll get sick

87
00:11:45,360 --> 00:11:46,800
if your head gets wet.

88
00:11:55,280 --> 00:11:57,720
This was taken on Phakorn's birthday.

89
00:12:04,040 --> 00:12:07,480
I embroidered a hat for each of them.

90
00:12:07,560 --> 00:12:11,080
Phakorn still has his. But Wee…

91
00:12:11,160 --> 00:12:15,000
probably lost his playing soccer.
I haven't seen it in ages.

92
00:12:28,680 --> 00:12:29,760
Aunt Da

93
00:12:30,520 --> 00:12:33,320
left Korn in your care
when he was just a baby?

94
00:12:34,280 --> 00:12:37,080
Yes, since he was an infant.

95
00:12:38,880 --> 00:12:40,400
How many months old was he?

96
00:12:43,560 --> 00:12:44,960
Six months.

97
00:12:48,000 --> 00:12:49,440
He was so little.

98
00:12:49,520 --> 00:12:53,440
Yes. I love him like my own son.

99
00:13:18,400 --> 00:13:20,520
IN OCTOBER 1999, THE COUPLE
WERE VACATIONING ON TAWAN ISLAND

100
00:13:26,000 --> 00:13:29,640
RELATIONSHIP TEST REPORT

101
00:13:29,720 --> 00:13:33,760
It happened in October.
Her son was six months old.

102
00:13:36,160 --> 00:13:38,200
But Korn was born in July.

103
00:13:40,120 --> 00:13:41,760
August, September, October.

104
00:13:44,240 --> 00:13:45,320
Three months.

105
00:13:52,640 --> 00:13:53,640
Was the report wrong?

106
00:13:56,320 --> 00:13:58,160
Or was it a different child?

107
00:14:11,400 --> 00:14:14,320
Taddao had a meeting
with the international team.

108
00:14:14,400 --> 00:14:15,840
She couldn't make it back in time.

109
00:14:16,400 --> 00:14:18,840
She asked me to bring these
for you to sign, Ms. Nada.

110
00:14:24,280 --> 00:14:27,600
Mr. Prajak came by your office today
to pick up some documents.

111
00:14:29,240 --> 00:14:32,760
Father called and told me.
What did he talk to you about?

112
00:14:33,400 --> 00:14:34,520
Just a few things.

113
00:14:40,240 --> 00:14:43,040
Has Phakorn been going to work?

114
00:14:48,440 --> 00:14:50,680
Rawee.

115
00:14:51,200 --> 00:14:54,080
I asked
if Phakorn's been going to the office.

116
00:14:57,120 --> 00:14:59,240
Phakorn just went to get something to eat

117
00:14:59,320 --> 00:15:01,120
when you woke up, Ms. Nada.

118
00:15:02,080 --> 00:15:04,480
He's been by your side
since you left the ICU.

119
00:15:08,120 --> 00:15:10,200
PROJECT OVERVIEW

120
00:15:14,480 --> 00:15:16,160
Please take care of this for me.

121
00:15:17,640 --> 00:15:18,960
Can you read my handwriting?

122
00:15:20,360 --> 00:15:23,680
Yes. I'll take it to Taddao right away.

123
00:15:45,200 --> 00:15:49,560
DR. THONGPHUM KHUMDEE

124
00:16:01,960 --> 00:16:03,000
PROJECT OVERVIEW BEFORE THE BOARD MEETING

125
00:16:03,080 --> 00:16:04,040
NEW PROJECT DESIGNS, THREE MORE OPTIONS
CANCEL THE MEETING WITH MS. DONRUDEE

126
00:16:04,120 --> 00:16:05,360
MAY 12 - DEAR DIARY,
TODAY I ALMOST CRIED IN FRONT OF FATHER

127
00:16:05,440 --> 00:16:06,640
EVERY TIME I SEE HIM,
HE ASKS ME TO WORK AT THE COMPANY

128
00:16:31,480 --> 00:16:33,640
Is there something
you want to talk to me about?

129
00:16:36,960 --> 00:16:39,000
Let's find somewhere quiet to talk.

130
00:17:46,760 --> 00:17:49,880
If you have something to confess,
out with it.

131
00:17:53,160 --> 00:17:56,000
Did you secretly have my blood
tested for DNA?

132
00:17:58,840 --> 00:18:03,120
Yes. And now I know you're not Nada's son.

133
00:18:06,880 --> 00:18:10,600
My father will hear about this.

134
00:18:14,760 --> 00:18:16,080
Get out now.

135
00:18:19,320 --> 00:18:21,720
Hey! What are you doing?

136
00:18:23,520 --> 00:18:25,440
Stop! Stop right now!

137
00:18:26,200 --> 00:18:27,280
Stop!

138
00:18:32,840 --> 00:18:34,560
Stop right now!

139
00:19:07,880 --> 00:19:08,920
Mr. Rawee.

140
00:19:10,080 --> 00:19:14,160
Yes? Is there something you need,
Ms. Alyssa?

141
00:19:19,360 --> 00:19:21,000
Could I speak to you in private

142
00:19:21,600 --> 00:19:23,800
after my meeting, Mr. Rawee?

143
00:19:25,600 --> 00:19:27,920
Yes, of course.

144
00:20:21,000 --> 00:20:23,840
-Let me get straight to the point.
-Of course.

145
00:20:25,520 --> 00:20:28,800
I need the DNA test results.
Please help me.

146
00:20:28,880 --> 00:20:31,720
For Ms. Nada and Mr. Phakorn?

147
00:20:32,320 --> 00:20:33,680
Rawee's too.

148
00:20:35,960 --> 00:20:37,920
I overheard

149
00:20:38,760 --> 00:20:41,440
that Ms. Pimpa ordered DNA tests
on you and Phakorn

150
00:20:41,960 --> 00:20:43,720
to compare with Aunt Da's.

151
00:20:46,520 --> 00:20:48,040
Why would Ms. Pimpa do that?

152
00:20:52,760 --> 00:20:53,840
Good question.

153
00:20:57,000 --> 00:20:59,600
I still haven't even changed
my surname to Tayawat.

154
00:21:01,080 --> 00:21:03,280
Mom still won't get the paperwork done.

155
00:21:04,000 --> 00:21:06,360
She's rich enough
to speed things up if she wants to.

156
00:21:07,240 --> 00:21:10,520
There's only one reason
she won't finish it.

157
00:21:11,200 --> 00:21:13,400
She knows I'm not her real son.

158
00:21:14,120 --> 00:21:16,600
If they don't accept you,
we can just keep living like this.

159
00:21:16,680 --> 00:21:19,240
You're healthy now.
You graduated overseas.

160
00:21:19,320 --> 00:21:21,200
You've gained so much already.
What more do you want?

161
00:21:21,280 --> 00:21:23,880
I've come too far, Wee. I can't go back…

162
00:21:25,920 --> 00:21:27,760
What exactly do you suspect?

163
00:21:29,920 --> 00:21:31,040
Do you think

164
00:21:31,720 --> 00:21:34,280
Korn is pretending to be Ms. Nada's son?

165
00:21:35,560 --> 00:21:36,480
Yes.

166
00:21:39,120 --> 00:21:40,720
According to the news reports,

167
00:21:41,600 --> 00:21:43,920
Aunt Da had her accident in October,

168
00:21:44,000 --> 00:21:46,200
the year you were both born.

169
00:21:46,280 --> 00:21:48,600
If Phakorn was born in July,

170
00:21:49,240 --> 00:21:51,440
he would've been three months old

171
00:21:52,480 --> 00:21:56,000
when Aunt Da left him with your mother,
not six.

172
00:21:58,200 --> 00:21:59,720
How did you find out about this?

173
00:22:01,880 --> 00:22:04,760
I happened to speak to Aunt Walai.

174
00:22:06,600 --> 00:22:08,280
Your mother confirmed

175
00:22:09,320 --> 00:22:11,440
Phakorn was six months old
when Aunt Da left him

176
00:22:12,080 --> 00:22:13,280
in her care.

177
00:22:18,800 --> 00:22:21,560
You two switched identities, didn't you?

178
00:22:50,920 --> 00:22:53,720
<i>If you have something to confess,</i>
<i>out with it.</i>

179
00:22:57,280 --> 00:23:00,120
Did you secretly have my blood
tested for DNA?

180
00:23:02,960 --> 00:23:07,240
Yes. And now I know you're not Nada's son.

181
00:23:11,800 --> 00:23:15,960
My father will hear about this.

182
00:23:19,720 --> 00:23:20,960
Get out now.

183
00:23:24,560 --> 00:23:26,960
Hey! What are you doing?

184
00:23:28,720 --> 00:23:30,480
Stop! Stop right now!

185
00:23:36,840 --> 00:23:37,840
Stop!

186
00:23:41,480 --> 00:23:42,320
Stop!

187
00:24:08,360 --> 00:24:11,240
Uh, Aunt?

188
00:24:11,800 --> 00:24:14,680
Aunt!

189
00:24:26,160 --> 00:24:27,560
She's still alive.

190
00:24:54,520 --> 00:24:55,440
Mom.

191
00:25:02,480 --> 00:25:03,960
Korn, what brings you here?

192
00:25:04,920 --> 00:25:09,400
Oh! Korn, what's wrong?

193
00:25:13,640 --> 00:25:14,600
Hey.

194
00:25:16,000 --> 00:25:18,040
What's wrong, Korn?

195
00:26:49,440 --> 00:26:50,400
Let me see that.

196
00:26:50,480 --> 00:26:52,840
-Wee, that's mine. Don't touch it.
-Hold on.

197
00:26:52,920 --> 00:26:55,400
Wait, Korn. Let me see it first.

198
00:26:56,000 --> 00:26:58,200
-No. Don't touch it.
-Wait, Korn.

199
00:26:59,080 --> 00:27:02,480
Who gave this to you?
It's got a little flower on it.

200
00:27:03,600 --> 00:27:06,160
It's been so long.
When are you going to give it back?

201
00:27:06,760 --> 00:27:08,040
Then let me keep it for now.

202
00:27:10,200 --> 00:27:13,160
Until you agree to be my girlfriend.

203
00:27:14,120 --> 00:27:17,320
And what if I don't say yes?

204
00:27:36,400 --> 00:27:38,840
Did Korn say why he went back?

205
00:27:40,760 --> 00:27:42,320
He said he missed home.

206
00:27:42,880 --> 00:27:45,520
Oh, Wee, I've finished tidying up.

207
00:27:45,600 --> 00:27:47,680
Have a look and see if it's okay.

208
00:27:48,480 --> 00:27:49,840
Everything looks good.

209
00:27:51,000 --> 00:27:53,280
Sorry I wasn't there to help.

210
00:27:54,160 --> 00:27:57,200
It's alright, Son.
Alyssa happened to drop by,

211
00:27:57,280 --> 00:28:00,040
<i>so we chatted while I tidied up.</i>
<i>It made the time fly.</i>

212
00:28:01,040 --> 00:28:04,040
What did you and Alyssa talk about, Mom?

213
00:28:04,720 --> 00:28:06,520
Well, she looked at the photos

214
00:28:06,600 --> 00:28:10,400
and a few other things.
She asked when Korn came to live with us.

215
00:28:10,480 --> 00:28:13,440
What did you tell her?

216
00:28:14,440 --> 00:28:16,000
I nearly let it slip,

217
00:28:16,080 --> 00:28:19,920
but I caught myself.
So I told her what was true for you.

218
00:28:20,000 --> 00:28:21,440
Six months old, right?

219
00:28:26,200 --> 00:28:27,400
I have to go now, dear.

220
00:28:30,880 --> 00:28:32,280
Are you hungry, Korn?

221
00:28:33,680 --> 00:28:34,520
Yes.

222
00:28:35,240 --> 00:28:36,920
I'll make you something to eat.

223
00:29:10,800 --> 00:29:13,760
<i>You two switched identities, didn't you?</i>

224
00:29:18,200 --> 00:29:21,760
Korn's birth records were altered.

225
00:29:22,560 --> 00:29:25,400
But I'd rather not go into the details.

226
00:29:26,360 --> 00:29:30,440
My father had to do it for Korn's safety.

227
00:29:32,120 --> 00:29:33,040
How so?

228
00:29:37,920 --> 00:29:40,240
<i>Kiat, take my son and run!</i>

229
00:29:41,560 --> 00:29:43,400
Before Mr. Rawich died,

230
00:29:44,040 --> 00:29:47,760
he called my father and insisted
that he take Korn and flee.

231
00:29:48,520 --> 00:29:52,120
My father had to conceal
Korn's birth records.

232
00:29:53,440 --> 00:29:55,440
Otherwise, he would've been killed too.

233
00:29:56,680 --> 00:29:58,840
The very lie you uncovered

234
00:30:00,040 --> 00:30:02,480
is what's kept Korn alive all these years.

235
00:30:15,600 --> 00:30:18,760
Is this all you asked me here
to talk about?

236
00:30:21,160 --> 00:30:22,880
I feel sorry for Korn.

237
00:30:22,960 --> 00:30:25,320
His girlfriend
doesn't understand him at all.

238
00:30:30,640 --> 00:30:32,720
I've told you my side of the story.

239
00:30:33,360 --> 00:30:36,080
Stop digging into my brother's past.

240
00:30:37,760 --> 00:30:40,960
If there's nothing else, please excuse me.

241
00:31:18,160 --> 00:31:19,680
Where's your sister?

242
00:31:20,760 --> 00:31:21,720
She's not answering her phone.

243
00:31:22,840 --> 00:31:24,840
How would I know, Father?

244
00:31:26,160 --> 00:31:27,920
You're useless.

245
00:31:40,960 --> 00:31:44,240
Da, did Pim visit you at the hospital?

246
00:31:45,600 --> 00:31:47,480
No, she hasn't, Father.

247
00:31:48,320 --> 00:31:52,120
<i>Where could she have gone?</i>
<i>I can't reach her.</i>

248
00:31:53,680 --> 00:31:55,800
Is something worrying you, Father?

249
00:32:28,440 --> 00:32:31,400
I should've hugged Dad
before he left for work.

250
00:32:35,600 --> 00:32:36,800
Go to sleep, Korn.

251
00:32:37,760 --> 00:32:41,240
Dad… I'm right here.

252
00:33:06,440 --> 00:33:07,360
Wee.

253
00:33:16,760 --> 00:33:17,880
Is something wrong?

254
00:34:08,440 --> 00:34:12,639
If only we could turn back time
and I hadn't gotten sick.

255
00:34:16,280 --> 00:34:17,800
This is weighing on you, isn't it?

256
00:34:23,199 --> 00:34:24,679
Do you think

257
00:34:24,760 --> 00:34:29,040
it's too late to tell the whole truth now?

258
00:34:32,639 --> 00:34:34,560
This isn't something
to take lightly, Korn.

259
00:34:35,280 --> 00:34:37,199
We need to talk it through with Mom.

260
00:34:38,239 --> 00:34:39,960
That way,
we can prepare for what's coming.

261
00:34:40,040 --> 00:34:42,280
Who knows what the consequences might be?

262
00:34:44,159 --> 00:34:46,560
You're her real son.

263
00:34:46,639 --> 00:34:49,719
If anything happens to me,
you have to help me, Wee.

264
00:34:49,800 --> 00:34:53,880
Of course.
Why wouldn't I help my own brother?

265
00:35:03,080 --> 00:35:07,120
Do you think I've changed, Wee?

266
00:35:09,720 --> 00:35:11,440
A little more handsome, maybe.

267
00:35:13,040 --> 00:35:16,760
That's not what I mean. I mean…

268
00:35:18,400 --> 00:35:20,800
Have I become a worse person?

269
00:35:21,960 --> 00:35:23,760
Why would you say that, Korn?

270
00:35:24,840 --> 00:35:26,840
No one stays the same forever.

271
00:35:27,720 --> 00:35:31,160
I've grown, and so have you.

272
00:35:31,960 --> 00:35:33,600
Even Ms. Nada has changed.

273
00:35:35,200 --> 00:35:36,480
How?

274
00:35:37,560 --> 00:35:39,880
I've read her diary.

275
00:35:40,520 --> 00:35:43,240
She said her dream
was to open a coffee shop.

276
00:35:43,960 --> 00:35:45,480
But in her latest interview,

277
00:35:46,200 --> 00:35:48,400
she said working for the company
was her dream.

278
00:35:49,360 --> 00:35:50,200
See?

279
00:35:51,440 --> 00:35:53,440
Even dreams can change.

280
00:35:54,280 --> 00:35:55,640
Even handwriting.

281
00:35:57,480 --> 00:36:00,920
Her handwriting? Mother's?

282
00:36:02,040 --> 00:36:02,880
Here.

283
00:36:06,400 --> 00:36:09,640
Look. Ms. Nada's handwriting now

284
00:36:09,720 --> 00:36:11,320
looks nothing like it does in her diary.

285
00:36:12,440 --> 00:36:14,480
Times change. People change.

286
00:36:15,320 --> 00:36:17,000
Don't overthink it, Korn.

287
00:36:18,160 --> 00:36:20,560
Let's get something to eat. I'm hungry.

288
00:36:44,640 --> 00:36:45,960
Here you go.

289
00:36:46,560 --> 00:36:49,040
I brought the handsome one today, Auntie.

290
00:36:50,680 --> 00:36:52,320
He was handsome even as a kid.

291
00:36:54,160 --> 00:36:57,400
So, who's more handsome, Auntie?
The older or the younger brother?

292
00:36:58,400 --> 00:36:59,560
You're both handsome.

293
00:37:00,560 --> 00:37:01,520
Thank you so much.

294
00:37:10,080 --> 00:37:11,880
No vegetables, no garlic.

295
00:37:11,960 --> 00:37:13,000
-No bean sprouts.
-No bean sprouts.

296
00:37:13,600 --> 00:37:14,640
Of course I remember.

297
00:37:33,760 --> 00:37:35,960
Should I tell Mom now, Wee?

298
00:37:38,240 --> 00:37:40,520
Don't you want to wait
until Ms. Nada's out of the hospital?

299
00:37:42,720 --> 00:37:45,200
I don't think I can wait that long.

300
00:37:47,880 --> 00:37:48,920
It's a shame.

301
00:37:49,840 --> 00:37:51,920
You fit right in with that family.

302
00:37:52,440 --> 00:37:54,840
I'd have a lot to adjust to.

303
00:37:57,080 --> 00:37:58,760
So would I.

304
00:38:00,160 --> 00:38:01,480
Adjust to what?

305
00:38:02,600 --> 00:38:04,400
You'd just be coming home.

306
00:38:08,520 --> 00:38:11,360
I've lived a different life
for years now, Wee.

307
00:38:12,120 --> 00:38:15,880
It's like having a car
and then having to take the bus.

308
00:38:15,960 --> 00:38:17,000
Do you understand?

309
00:38:19,000 --> 00:38:22,320
It's not that bad. Don't forget,

310
00:38:22,400 --> 00:38:25,240
you weren't born in heaven
and suddenly fell from it.

311
00:38:26,800 --> 00:38:28,960
You're just coming back
to where you started.

312
00:38:34,280 --> 00:38:36,840
You've eaten noodles at stalls like this
since you were a kid.

313
00:38:37,560 --> 00:38:39,760
We used to be happy living like this.

314
00:38:40,680 --> 00:38:41,840
Don't get too attached.

315
00:38:44,000 --> 00:38:46,200
Think of it as a trade for peace of mind.

316
00:38:50,520 --> 00:38:53,120
I just hope things don't get any worse.

317
00:38:54,040 --> 00:38:55,320
They won't.

318
00:38:56,600 --> 00:38:58,200
You've got me.

319
00:38:58,880 --> 00:39:01,520
I'd never let my brother struggle.

320
00:39:06,320 --> 00:39:07,880
You don't have to worry.

321
00:39:23,600 --> 00:39:26,880
Could Mr. Rawee not know
he's her real son?

322
00:39:36,960 --> 00:39:39,320
Am I meddling too much
in other people's lives?

323
00:39:43,960 --> 00:39:44,920
Ow.

324
00:39:46,760 --> 00:39:49,320
Dad! He's been shot.

325
00:39:49,400 --> 00:39:51,320
This isn't Rawee's fault at all.

326
00:39:52,480 --> 00:39:54,680
If you knew that boy might lose his future

327
00:39:54,760 --> 00:39:56,960
as a national football player
because he saved Alyssa,

328
00:39:57,560 --> 00:39:58,960
would you still say something like this?

329
00:39:59,640 --> 00:40:03,440
If my father were still alive,
he'd probably say

330
00:40:04,600 --> 00:40:07,760
this was karma bringing us together,

331
00:40:08,880 --> 00:40:10,360
so we could make things right.

332
00:40:12,000 --> 00:40:13,800
And now, this is where it ends.

333
00:40:24,400 --> 00:40:26,280
But I want you to know

334
00:40:26,920 --> 00:40:28,320
that I'm serious.

335
00:40:29,440 --> 00:40:31,800
And I really like you.

336
00:40:34,320 --> 00:40:35,520
Then let me keep it for now.

337
00:40:37,840 --> 00:40:40,720
Until you agree to be my girlfriend.

338
00:40:41,320 --> 00:40:44,360
And what if I don't say yes?

339
00:40:45,000 --> 00:40:46,160
Then…

340
00:40:50,120 --> 00:40:51,680
I can wait my whole life.

341
00:41:35,320 --> 00:41:37,520
Oh, Mom. Haven't you gone to the shop yet?

342
00:41:38,240 --> 00:41:39,880
I sent Somphit ahead.

343
00:41:39,960 --> 00:41:42,960
She's good now. I can leave it to her.
Where's your brother?

344
00:41:43,040 --> 00:41:44,760
He's coming down.

345
00:41:44,840 --> 00:41:47,040
<i>Today's breaking news. Pimpa Tayawat</i>

346
00:41:47,120 --> 00:41:49,480
<i>has vanished without a trace.</i>

347
00:41:50,080 --> 00:41:51,680
It's about Ms. Pimpa, Mom.

348
00:41:51,760 --> 00:41:53,800
Turn it up, Son.

349
00:41:55,000 --> 00:41:58,040
<i>Pimpa Tayawat, daughter of Prajak Tayawat,</i>

350
00:41:58,120 --> 00:42:01,040
<i>owner of the multibillion-baht</i>
<i>Tayawat Group,</i>

351
00:42:01,120 --> 00:42:03,680
<i>has vanished without a trace.</i>

352
00:42:09,320 --> 00:42:10,680
Missing?

353
00:42:12,600 --> 00:42:13,720
How is that possible?

354
00:42:14,320 --> 00:42:16,160
<i>Panas Tayawat,</i>

355
00:42:16,240 --> 00:42:20,080
<i>her younger brother,</i>
<i>has reported her disappearance.</i>

356
00:42:20,160 --> 00:42:24,040
<i>She disappeared yesterday morning.</i>
<i>He's been unable to reach her.</i>

357
00:42:34,800 --> 00:42:36,040
So…

358
00:42:37,640 --> 00:42:39,680
The secret's still safe.

359
00:42:46,200 --> 00:42:49,440
<i>CCTV footage suggests the last person</i>

360
00:42:49,520 --> 00:42:54,280
<i>with Pimpa</i>
<i>was her nephew, Phakorn Tayawat.</i>

361
00:43:29,720 --> 00:43:31,680
Could this be connected to the DNA tests?

362
00:43:39,280 --> 00:43:41,600
Korn!

363
00:43:41,680 --> 00:43:44,640
Korn, what's going on? Tell me.

364
00:43:44,720 --> 00:43:46,080
It's nothing, Mom.

365
00:43:46,160 --> 00:43:49,080
I just stopped by to update Aunt Pim
on Mother's condition. That's all.

366
00:43:50,760 --> 00:43:53,520
Listen, go give your statement
to the police right away.

367
00:43:53,600 --> 00:43:57,440
Call me as soon as you're done, Son.

368
00:43:58,520 --> 00:43:59,720
Yes, Mom.

369
00:44:02,440 --> 00:44:05,960
Wee, take the day off
and go with your brother.

370
00:44:06,040 --> 00:44:09,280
You have a law degree,
so you can help him if he needs it.

371
00:44:10,760 --> 00:44:11,640
Okay.

372
00:44:19,960 --> 00:44:20,800
Korn.

373
00:44:24,040 --> 00:44:27,640
Where did you go
after you left the office?

374
00:44:28,240 --> 00:44:29,720
Try to remember.

375
00:44:35,840 --> 00:44:37,480
If someone can vouch for you,

376
00:44:38,080 --> 00:44:39,760
that could clear you of suspicion.

377
00:44:40,840 --> 00:44:43,120
Like last night,
Mom and I can vouch for you.

378
00:44:43,200 --> 00:44:45,160
You did spend the night at home.

379
00:44:55,560 --> 00:44:57,040
Mr. Prajak is on the phone.

380
00:45:00,040 --> 00:45:01,200
Yes, Father?

381
00:45:04,680 --> 00:45:05,960
What did you say?

382
00:45:10,200 --> 00:45:11,920
Pim is dead?

383
00:45:15,600 --> 00:45:18,120
<i>Evidence found on the body</i>

384
00:45:18,200 --> 00:45:21,080
<i>and confirmation from her father,</i>
<i>Mr. Prajak Tayawat,</i>

385
00:45:21,160 --> 00:45:23,960
<i>have identified the woman</i>
<i>who died under mysterious circumstances</i>

386
00:45:24,040 --> 00:45:25,760
<i>as Pimpa Tayawat.</i>

387
00:45:30,400 --> 00:45:33,680
Alyssa, something terrible has happened.

388
00:45:34,920 --> 00:45:36,600
Is it about Ms. Pimpa?

389
00:45:37,320 --> 00:45:38,520
Yes.

390
00:45:39,240 --> 00:45:42,480
I can't believe it.
We saw each other so recently.

391
00:45:43,000 --> 00:45:44,120
Then suddenly…

392
00:45:45,600 --> 00:45:47,600
she was murdered.

393
00:45:53,960 --> 00:45:55,240
It's okay.

394
00:46:02,400 --> 00:46:04,880
<i>Have you seen the news about Ms. Pimpa?</i>

395
00:46:05,600 --> 00:46:08,880
Yes. What are you calling about?

396
00:46:11,800 --> 00:46:14,360
Do you think Ms. Pimpa's death

397
00:46:14,440 --> 00:46:17,880
has anything to do with her ordering
DNA tests on you and your brother?

398
00:46:19,680 --> 00:46:21,880
Just say what you're trying to say.

399
00:46:22,800 --> 00:46:24,240
Please don't get angry.

400
00:46:24,920 --> 00:46:27,000
I'm only calling to warn you.

401
00:46:27,080 --> 00:46:28,960
If the police find out about this,

402
00:46:29,720 --> 00:46:31,920
your brother will look very suspicious.

403
00:46:32,760 --> 00:46:34,960
Make sure you have evidence to clear him.

404
00:46:36,600 --> 00:46:40,600
No way.
Korn isn't cruel enough to kill anyone.

405
00:46:43,160 --> 00:46:45,360
I don't think Korn did it either.

406
00:46:46,800 --> 00:46:48,520
I just want you to be prepared.

407
00:47:10,320 --> 00:47:12,400
I did meet my aunt at the office.

408
00:47:13,000 --> 00:47:15,440
We talked about my mother's condition.

409
00:47:16,200 --> 00:47:18,200
Then we went our separate ways.

410
00:47:18,880 --> 00:47:20,320
We didn't leave in the same car.

411
00:47:23,560 --> 00:47:26,760
We're not actually that close,

412
00:47:26,840 --> 00:47:29,280
so I didn't ask where she was going next.

413
00:47:29,360 --> 00:47:30,560
I went to check at the company.

414
00:47:30,640 --> 00:47:33,560
Are there no CCTV cameras
on the executive floor?

415
00:47:36,000 --> 00:47:36,840
That's right.

416
00:47:40,440 --> 00:47:42,200
Do you know why, Mr. Phakorn?

417
00:47:44,040 --> 00:47:45,680
Grandfather said

418
00:47:46,320 --> 00:47:49,880
he didn't want
company matters getting out.

419
00:47:50,480 --> 00:47:54,440
Did Ms. Pimpa have any conflicts
with anyone at the company?

420
00:47:56,840 --> 00:47:59,280
Grandfather removed her from the board

421
00:47:59,360 --> 00:48:01,520
because of mismanagement.

422
00:48:01,600 --> 00:48:03,440
Apart from that…

423
00:48:05,080 --> 00:48:07,160
I'm not aware of any other conflicts.

424
00:48:11,120 --> 00:48:12,400
How did it go, Korn?

425
00:48:14,120 --> 00:48:15,720
I just gave my statement.

426
00:48:16,720 --> 00:48:20,680
But if they ask you, you have to tell them
I went home and spent the night there.

427
00:48:21,400 --> 00:48:24,840
Don't worry, Korn. What about Ms. Nada?

428
00:48:25,560 --> 00:48:27,400
She's giving her statement.

429
00:48:28,280 --> 00:48:31,120
Taddao called me in
to take care of some work at the office.

430
00:48:31,200 --> 00:48:33,040
I have to leave first.

431
00:48:33,120 --> 00:48:34,680
Will you be okay on your own?

432
00:48:37,080 --> 00:48:37,920
Yes.

433
00:48:46,640 --> 00:48:47,520
I'll get going, then.

434
00:48:59,520 --> 00:49:00,600
Wee.

435
00:49:01,200 --> 00:49:03,320
I'm taking these files
to Ms. Nada to sign.

436
00:49:03,400 --> 00:49:06,120
Could you print all of this
and bind it for me?

437
00:49:06,200 --> 00:49:08,160
-I'm counting on you, Wee.
-Sure.

438
00:49:08,240 --> 00:49:09,800
Thanks so much. You'll finish a bit late.

439
00:49:09,880 --> 00:49:11,160
No problem.

440
00:49:44,360 --> 00:49:45,360
Mom.

441
00:49:46,640 --> 00:49:47,480
Mom.

442
00:49:49,600 --> 00:49:51,800
Huh? Are we home?

443
00:49:51,880 --> 00:49:54,720
Yes. Go upstairs and get some rest.

444
00:49:54,800 --> 00:49:56,040
I'll go see Wee.

445
00:49:58,240 --> 00:49:59,520
Mom.

446
00:50:00,200 --> 00:50:04,240
Before all this happened,
did you talk to Aunt Pim?

447
00:50:05,920 --> 00:50:06,840
No.

448
00:50:08,680 --> 00:50:11,080
No calls?
You didn't discuss anything at all?

449
00:50:12,360 --> 00:50:13,240
No.

450
00:50:14,320 --> 00:50:16,080
But the police said

451
00:50:17,080 --> 00:50:19,440
Pim visited me at the hospital.

452
00:50:20,000 --> 00:50:21,240
I must have been asleep.

453
00:50:25,400 --> 00:50:26,240
Okay.

454
00:50:28,440 --> 00:50:32,520
What did the police ask you?

455
00:50:33,240 --> 00:50:35,080
About the timeline.

456
00:50:35,720 --> 00:50:37,840
I saw Aunt Pim at the office
the other day.

457
00:50:37,920 --> 00:50:41,640
They also asked
about conflicts in the family.

458
00:50:42,720 --> 00:50:44,480
What did you tell them?

459
00:50:45,600 --> 00:50:47,440
I told them the truth.

460
00:50:49,120 --> 00:50:50,160
I didn't know of any.

461
00:50:51,600 --> 00:50:54,000
I had no problem with her.

462
00:50:54,080 --> 00:50:56,200
She was the one who hated me.

463
00:50:59,720 --> 00:51:01,360
Don't overthink it, Korn.

464
00:51:02,080 --> 00:51:03,760
Go on, and come back soon.

465
00:51:04,400 --> 00:51:05,240
Okay.

466
00:53:34,320 --> 00:53:37,400
Sir, would you like me to come with you?

467
00:53:38,520 --> 00:53:40,760
No. Wait in the car.

468
00:54:11,320 --> 00:54:12,400
Sir.

469
00:54:22,600 --> 00:54:24,680
Oh, Rawich.

470
00:54:31,720 --> 00:54:34,680
No, that's not right.
What's your name again?

471
00:54:35,560 --> 00:54:36,920
Rawee, Sir.

472
00:54:39,400 --> 00:54:41,680
Yes, Rawee.

473
00:55:23,960 --> 00:55:26,200
I've just finished my work.

474
00:55:26,840 --> 00:55:29,400
Did you need something
from Ms. Pimpa's office?

475
00:55:29,480 --> 00:55:31,000
Is that why you're here so late?

476
00:55:31,680 --> 00:55:33,280
I just miss my daughter.

477
00:56:14,720 --> 00:56:15,560
Excuse me, Sir.

478
00:56:19,600 --> 00:56:21,920
You'd been inside a while,
so I came to check on you.

479
00:56:25,520 --> 00:56:27,800
Sir, I think

480
00:56:28,400 --> 00:56:30,800
you should go home and get some rest.

481
00:57:17,120 --> 00:57:18,120
Come out, Korn.

482
00:57:35,840 --> 00:57:38,520
<i>What do you think Grandfather</i>
<i>was looking for in Aunt Pim's office?</i>

483
00:57:39,080 --> 00:57:41,080
<i>Maybe he just misses his daughter.</i>

484
00:57:42,200 --> 00:57:44,120
You seem to understand him so well.

485
00:57:44,680 --> 00:57:46,760
Must be that DNA you share
as grandfather and grandson.

486
00:57:46,840 --> 00:57:48,680
Are you really going to stop here, Korn?

487
00:57:48,760 --> 00:57:50,760
<i>When will you tell everyone the truth?</i>

488
00:57:51,480 --> 00:57:53,120
Korn, go with Grandfather.

489
00:57:53,200 --> 00:57:54,320
Yes.

490
00:57:54,400 --> 00:57:55,680
Rawee can take me.

491
00:57:57,360 --> 00:58:00,240
Korn can stay
and help look after the guests.

492
00:58:01,040 --> 00:58:03,560
Why did Grandfather call you over earlier?

493
00:58:03,640 --> 00:58:05,960
He just offered me a job as an assistant.

494
00:58:06,040 --> 00:58:08,640
An assistant? Whose assistant?

495
00:58:08,720 --> 00:58:10,520
<i>His assistant?</i>

496
00:58:10,600 --> 00:58:13,600
I'd like to talk to you, Grandfather.

497
00:58:13,680 --> 00:58:17,960
Why do you seem to value Wee more than me?

498
00:58:20,840 --> 00:58:23,440
Are you really my grandson?

499
00:59:02,680 --> 00:59:05,280
Subtitle translation by:
Chomchanach Yanaharn
